-- title:
--   Supporting fact for Theorem 7.13, not in the paper — for every D, ω, (k_n) and β, the measure μ_β of (7.11) on G_ω is non-degenerate
-- statement:
--   For every natural number $D$, every string $\omega$, every sequence $(k_n)$ of natural numbers and every real $\beta$, the measure $\mu_\beta$ on $G_\omega$ of (7.11) (`muBeta D ω k β`) is non-degenerate (`IsNondegenerate`): the subsemigroup of $G_\omega$ generated by $\{g : \mu_\beta(g) \ne 0\}$ is all of $G_\omega$. No hypothesis on $D$, $\omega$, $(k_n)$ or $\beta$ is assumed.
--
--   This is not a result of the paper. With `ErschlerZheng.hasNontrivialPoissonBoundary_iff_exists_bounded_isHarmonic_ne_of_isNondegenerate` it backs the sentence of the note on `ErschlerZheng.hasNontrivialPoissonBoundary_muBeta` saying that the set of products of elements of the support of $\mu_\beta$ is all of $G_\omega$, so that for $\mu_\beta$ the definition `HasNontrivialPoissonBoundary` is the criterion of p. 2 and Theorem 7.13 says what the paper says.
-- source:
--   Erschler, A. and Zheng, T., Growth of periodic Grigorchuk groups, Invent. Math. 219 (2020) 1069–1155, https://doi.org/10.1007/s00222-019-00922-0 (arXiv:1802.09077v2, whose page numbers are used), p. 9, μ_β is non-degenerate (supporting fact, not in the paper)

